From 26d0b7850a7dcedf9b7154b2b59393a5a6547d55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ashallowperson <245951141+ashallowperson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] BatteryService: scale mis-scaled charge capacity by 10x

The MTK kernel gauge (tc_gauge/tran-auto-test) on the Tecno CM6 reports
charge_full and charge_full_design in 0.01 mAh units (e.g. 520000 for a
5200 mAh cell) instead of the uAh units expected by AOSP.  As a result,
BatteryService exposes EXTRA_DESIGN_CAPACITY = 520000 and
EXTRA_MAXIMUM_CAPACITY = 520000, which every consumer interprets as
520 mAh -- a 10x underestimate.

Detect the mis-scaled values (positive but < 1000000 uAh, i.e. < 1000
mAh -- no real phone battery is that small) and scale them 10x so the
broadcast, dumpsys battery, GMS, and third-party apps all see the correct
5200000 uAh (5200 mAh).

The kernel gauge driver is a prebuilt module that cannot be rebuilt, so
this framework-level compensation is the safest fix.  The health HAL
(MTK proprietary android.hardware.health-service.mediatek) is untouched,
preserving fast charging and the offline charger screen.
---
 .../core/java/com/android/server/BatteryService.java | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/BatteryService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/BatteryService.java
index 4eeec8b99..77155d2d4 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/BatteryService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/BatteryService.java
@@ -754,6 +754,18 @@ public final class BatteryService extends SystemService {
 
         synchronized (mLock) {
             if (!mUpdatesStopped) {
+                // MTK kernel gauge quirk: charge_full / charge_full_design
+                // reported in 0.01 mAh units instead of µAh.  Scale ×10
+                // so that EXTRA_DESIGN_CAPACITY and EXTRA_MAXIMUM_CAPACITY
+                // carry the correct µAh value.
+                if (info.batteryFullChargeUah > 0
+                        && info.batteryFullChargeUah < 1000000) {
+                    info.batteryFullChargeUah *= 10;
+                }
+                if (info.batteryFullChargeDesignCapacityUah > 0
+                        && info.batteryFullChargeDesignCapacityUah < 1000000) {
+                    info.batteryFullChargeDesignCapacityUah *= 10;
+                }
                 mHealthInfo = info;
                 // Process the new values.
                 processValuesLocked(false);
-- 
